================================================================================
MyChangeLog.log  --  Personal change log for my YADE fork.
================================================================================

FORMAT: each entry STARTS WITH A DATE [YYYY-MM-DD]. Append new entries under
"=== LOG ===", newest LAST. This file tracks ANY change I make to this fork
(engines, recorders, docs, ...). Entries describe the final state of the change
set, not the step-by-step editing history.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=== LOG ===   (chronological, each entry begins with [YYYY-MM-DD], newest LAST)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[2026-10-12]
  This commit is the V2.0.0 release of this fork: one version, one commit. A
  dedicated git tag V2.0.0 is created by this commit.

  --- Contents ---
  The release adds two capability groups on top of the upstream yade baseline this
  branch is built on.

  1) DirectShear suite -- rigid direct-shear / interface-shear boundary control.
  The engine had already been used and validated in production runs before this
  release, so it is packaged here essentially as it stands (comments / docs
  clarified, plus one typo fix, intiald50 -> initiald50 in DirectShearBox.cpp):
  - pkg/common/Recorder.hpp : Recorder::out made public (was protected) so
    DirectShearBoxRecorder can reuse the same output stream.
  - pkg/dem/DirectShearBox.hpp / .cpp : ADDED. DirectShearBox base engine and its
    DirectShearBox6D subclass (rigid shear-box boundary control). Public surface:
      * stress servo      : controlExternalStress(), controlInternalStress(),
                            computeStress(), ComputeUnbalancedForce();
      * particle scaling  : growParticles() override (mass/dynamicOnly options);
      * friction control  : setBodyFriction(), setBodiesFriction(),
                            setWallFriction(), setWallsFriction(),
                            setSpheresFriction()/setSpheresFrictionOnly(),
                            setAllFriction(), updateInteractionsFriction(),
                            setInteractionsFrictionOnBody/Bodies/Walls/Clump();
      * rolling & twist damping (eta) : setBodyEtaRoll/Twist(), setBodiesEta*(),
                            setWallEtaRoll/Twist(), setWallsEta*(),
                            setSpheresEtaRoll/Twist(Only)(), setAllEta(),
                            setInteractionsEta();
      * loading control   : setCycle(), setLoading(), setY(), setV(),
                            setCurrentVY()/getCurrentVY(), setGravityZ(), setAxial(),
                            setExternal(), setDamping(), resetRefSe3(), setPipeDOFs();
      * boundary / runtime: updateStiffness(), action() main loop, showState(),
                            setcolors();
      * multi-body walls (wall_ids_*) and periodic-boundary-friendly setup that
        pairs with InsertionSortCollider's allowBiggerThanPeriod.
    updateStiffness() and the particlesVolume summation are OpenMP-parallel
    (thread-local accumulation + omp critical / reduction(+:...)); the Z0 / Z1
    Body and State pointers, the inverse X / Y / Z surface areas and the current
    heightZ are cached (cachedWallZ0/Z1, cachedStateZ0/Z1, cachedHeightZ,
    cachedInvXSurface/cachedInvYSurface/cachedInvZSurface) and re-derived only
    when they are missing or when the height changed; setInteractionsFrictionOnBodies()
    uses an std::unordered_set lookup instead of a linear scan over bodyIDs; the
    vestigial "#ifdef FLOW_ENGINE ... flowEngine_T.hpp" block is dropped (no Flow
    / pfv symbol is used anywhere in the file) and <unordered_set> is included
    explicitly; currentSaverNum is no longer Attr::readonly, i.e. it can be
    assigned from Python (reading it is unchanged).
  - pkg/dem/DirectShearBoxRecorder.hpp / .cpp : ADDED. Records the six-face stress
    / displacement of the direct-shear box (one CSV line per iterPeriod) with
    multi-file saving (file2) and a scalingFactor hook. The engine lookup caches
    getClassName() and stops at the first DirectShearBox / DirectShearBox6D engine
    found, and the wall_id_Z1 State pointer is resolved once. The CSV header and
    the column order are unchanged.
  - pkg/dem/timeSaver.hpp / .cpp : ADDED. Periodic snapshot-saving engine
    (setCycle / setSavertime / setSaverEvery).

  2) Capillary model for the 6D (cohesive-frictional) contact model.
  The capillary law only worked with CapillaryPhys / MindlinCapillaryPhys; this
  release adds CapillaryCohPhys and Law2_ScGeom6D_CapillaryCohPhys_Capillarity, so
  meniscus (liquid bridge) effects can be computed on ScGeom6D interactions as
  well:
  - pkg/dem/CapillaryPhys.hpp / .cpp : ADDED CapillaryCohPhys, the capillary
    interaction physics (IPhys) for cohesive-frictional contacts. It is
    CohFrictPhys based -- so it also carries the normal / tangential cohesion
    and the rolling / twisting stiffness -- and exposes the same liquid-bridge
    fields as CapillaryPhys: meniscus, isBroken, capillaryPressure, vMeniscus,
    Delta1, Delta2, fCap, fusionNumber, nn11 / nn33, currentIndexes. Its IPhys
    functor Ip2_CohFrictMat_CohFrictMat_CapillaryCohPhys (also added, derived
    from Ip2_CohFrictMat_CohFrictMat_CohFrictPhys) creates it for CohFrictMat /
    CohFrictMat interactions. Both are registered in YADE_PLUGIN.
  - pkg/dem/Law2_ScGeom6D_CapillaryCohPhys_Capillarity.hpp / .cpp : ADDED. The
    6D counterpart of Law2_ScGeom_CapillaryPhys_Capillarity, for CapillaryCohPhys
    + ScGeom6D interactions. It reads the same M(r=i) capillary files and uses the
    same control parameter (capillaryPressure), the same surfaceTension and the
    same fusion logic (fusionDetection / binaryFusion), but keeps its own
    BodiesMenisciiList6D container for the menisci-overlap bookkeeping.
  - pkg/dem/Law2_ScGeom_CapillaryPhys_Capillarity.hpp : BodiesMenisciiList,
    capillarylaw and the law class itself got virtual destructors, and
    checkFusion() became virtual, so that the 6D law can derive from it.
  - preprocessing/dem/Shop.hpp / Shop_02.cpp : new helpers
      * getCapillaryStressNew() : Love-Weber capillary stress computed from
        CapillaryCohPhys (sphere-sphere interactions only);
      * capillaryCalculation() : single-pass aggregation of the six homogenised
        stress components, the capillary pressure and the water saturation (%);
      * setFrictionEtaRoll() : set the rolling friction (eta) and the friction
        angle in one call;
      * growParticlesWithInteractions() / growParticlesWith6DInteractions() :
        homothetic particle growth which also updates the (6D) interactions.
  - py/_utils.cpp : those five functions are exposed to python
    (getCapillaryStressNew, capillaryCalculation, setFrictionEtaRoll,
    growParticlesWithInteractions, growParticlesWith6DInteractions).
  One deliberate functional divergence: the existing Shop::getCapillaryStress()
  had been extended in place elsewhere so that it would also handle
  CapillaryCohPhys. This release does NOT touch getCapillaryStress() -- the
  original function is kept exactly as it was -- and adds a NEW function
  Shop::getCapillaryStressNew() beside it (together with
  Shop::capillaryCalculation()).

